\ A quotation survives an if-merge: the chosen arm pushes a quotation [10]/[20]
\ without calling it, so it escapes the merge as the word output. The merge reifies
\ each arm's surviving quotation into the shared slot (closing the stale-raw_at_slot
\ hazard) and the result is callable interpreter-free.
pick-quot: ( flag -- q ) [ [ [ 10 ] ] [ [ 20 ] ] if ] ;

t pick-quot call .
f pick-quot call .
